---
// How OpenHAL relates to Anthropic's Model Hardware Standard. Facts come from docs/research only.
---

<div class="mhs">
  <p class="statement">
    <span>MHS is for labs, in a closed preview.</span>
    <span>OpenHAL is open and works today.</span>
    <span>We plan to be compatible.</span>
  </p>
  <div class="facts">
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt class="legend">MHS</dt>
        <dd>
          Anthropic previewed the Model Hardware Standard on August 27, 2026, for labs and advanced manufacturing. It is a limited research
          preview. Access is by application, and there is no public spec, schema or SDK yet.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="legend">OpenHAL</dt>
        <dd>
          Open source under Apache 2.0, for makers, teaching labs and small labs. It uses the same idea of read and write commands with
          enforced limits, so device files can map onto MHS once its spec is public.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p><a href="/spec/mhs-mapping/">How the spec maps onto MHS today</a></p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .mhs {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-6);
  }

  .statement {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-1);
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--t-4);
    line-height: var(--lh-4);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }

  .statement span:last-child {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }

  dl > div {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-1);
    padding-top: var(--s-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .facts > p {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .mhs {
      grid-template-columns: 6fr 6fr;
      gap: var(--s-7);
    }
  }
</style>
